---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 3.6 · Blood Moon Rises & Graduation" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="3-6" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 3.6 · final mandatory page</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Blood Moon Rises &amp; Graduation</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Apply the quest XP you have already earned, close only the live Blood Moon skill gaps, finish the Myreque story, and claim your Quest Cape. After that, the route belongs to you.</p>
      </header>
      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Live Woodcutting, Smithing, Cooking and Fletching remainders → The Blood Moon Rises → all-green quest journal → Quest Cape."
        stats={["Actual 74 Woodcutting", "Actual 72 Smithing and Cooking", "Actual 70 Fletching; the other six nonboostable gates already carry in"]}
        unlocks={["Vampyrium, Hallowed flail and Sunspear", "Quest point cape and hood after every released quest is green", "No mandatory Bowfa, Slayer-unique, raid or post-quest boss farm"]}
      />
      <div class="callout"><strong>Start with the real 3.5 exit.</strong> Dragon Slayer II's 80,000 Smithing XP has already landed; the Curse of the Empty Lord museum lamp normally went to Fletching; the route also owns 74+ Slayer, 75+ Magic/Ranged, Fire Cape, Barrows gloves, Piety and the ordinary quest/travel kit. None of those rewards may be counted a second time. Read the <em>live skill tab</em> before cutting, smithing, cooking or fletching anything.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Final four skill gates · live-XP dashboard</div><h2>Train the remainder, not a planning-account estimate.</h2>
        <p>For each skill below, remaining XP is <strong>max(0, target XP − your current XP)</strong>. The skill tab already shows the level and XP; use it. If a skill is already at or above its target, mark its outcome complete and skip its training. The four targets are hard Blood Moon entry gates, not aspirational endgame goals.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Woodcutting 74:</strong> max(0, <strong>1,096,278</strong> − live Woodcutting XP).</li>
          <li><strong>Smithing 72:</strong> max(0, <strong>899,257</strong> − live Smithing XP), <em>after</em> DS2's 80,000 XP.</li>
          <li><strong>Cooking 72:</strong> max(0, <strong>899,257</strong> − live Cooking XP).</li>
          <li><strong>Fletching 70:</strong> max(0, <strong>737,627</strong> − live Fletching XP), including any earlier quest XP and the museum lamp if allocated there.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <RouteStep id="i36-woodcutting" number="1" title="Reach actual 74 Woodcutting, then stop">
        <p>The route guarantees actual 70 already. <strong>Sulliusceps</strong> on Fossil Island are the familiar active/low-attention overlap taught in Chapter 1; keep useful fossils or caps, but do not wait for another cap drop. For a calmer session, cut normal Forestry trees, teaks, maples or yews wherever your travel and bank make sense. A conventional faster method is fine if you enjoy it, but no 2-tick/1.5-tick cycle is assumed. The quest consumes <strong>actual 74</strong>; 80, 90 or 99 gives no mandatory benefit here.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-smithing" number="2" title="Reach actual 72 Smithing from the post-DS2 XP total">
        <p>Check the Smithing tab <em>after</em> the fixed DS2 reward. Take only the live remainder to 72. <strong>Giants' Foundry</strong>, already introduced earlier, converts spare banked metal into Smithing XP and direct coins. Do not smelt away bars reserved for ammunition, quests, Sailing or another known consumer. Ordinary banked bars at an anvil or another comfortable method are fine. Stop at <strong>actual 72</strong>; 73 is only a separate, bank-conditional adamant-bolt production level from 3.3, not a Blood Moon requirement.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-cooking" number="3" title="Reach actual 72 Cooking and leave useful food behind">
        <p>Cook banked raw fish or karambwans at a convenient range. If the bank is short, catch more karambwans or other useful fish and turn this small gate into real boss food. Read current XP before choosing quantities; do not follow a fixed fish bill. Stop at <strong>actual 72</strong>. No 1-tick cooking or tick manipulation is required.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-fletching" number="4" title="Reach actual 70 Fletching using the bank you actually have">
        <p>This may be the largest remaining bill, but earlier quest XP, Devious Minds, any conditional bolt production and the <strong>10,000-XP Curse of the Empty Lord museum lamp by default</strong> already affect your live total. Make the best sensible <strong>unstrung bows from banked maple, yew or other useful logs</strong>. Kingdom maples can help if present; no fixed kingdom stock is assumed. Banked unfinished bows, shafts, feathers or spare bars/darts are alternatives, but preserve combat ammunition.</p>
        <p>If <strong>Broader Fletching</strong> is already unlocked, broad arrows are a faster/resource-spending option. If not, weigh the permanent unlock against your actual Slayer-point balance; this page does <em>not</em> automatically spend 300 points to unlock it. No tick manipulation. Stop at <strong>actual 70</strong>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Blood Moon Rises · nonboostable preflight</div><h2>Confirm the quest can start before packing for it.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i36-preflight" number="5" title="Verify every Blood Moon gate and prepare the first inventory">
        <p>Read actual levels in the skill tab: <strong>74 Slayer, 74 Woodcutting, 72 Smithing, 72 Cooking, 70 Fletching, 66 Mining, 65 Hunter, 64 Crafting, 64 Herblore and 57 Magic</strong>. These ten gates are <strong>not boostable</strong>. The route already covers the last six (including Slayer) and the four new outcomes above cover the rest, but check them all. Confirm <strong>Sins of the Father</strong> and <strong>A Night at the Theatre</strong> are green. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Blood_Moon_Rises" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current quest requirements and phase guide</a>.</p>
        <p>Bank-check the <strong>Blisterwood flail</strong>, Drakan's medallion, Vyre noble clothes, ordinary melee/defensive armour, Fire Cape, Barrows gloves, dragon defender, food, Prayer restores, run energy and an exit/travel plan. The flail is retained from Sins of the Father; if it is missing, take <strong>40,000 coins</strong> to buy a replacement from Ivan at the Meiyerditch Myreque hideout. Noble clothes can be recovered free from its chest. Pack a tinderbox and pickaxe if convenient; the quest can supply those, plus the later hammer, knife, chisel and blisterwood logs. Re-bank by phase rather than carrying every tool at once. No rare weapon or boss unique is an entry condition.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-early-story" number="6" title="Start with Sarius, reach Vampyrium and survive the Blood Hunt">
        <p>Travel to the <strong>Icyene Graveyard</strong> (boat from southern Burgh de Rott or Meiyerditch, or approach from Slepe) and speak to <strong>Sarius Guile</strong>. Regroup with Ivan at the hideout beneath Old Man Ral's house. Wear the Vyre noble clothes for the opening infiltration and defend Ivan: use Protect from Melee, tag attackers off him and prioritise dangerous sentinels/bloodvelds. The quest then moves through <strong>Paterdomus, a portal into Vampyrium, Castle Drakan's key/clock puzzles and haemalchemic stockpile</strong>. Follow Quest Helper or the linked quest guide for exact puzzle clicks; keep inventory space and bank when the story returns you to a supply point.</p>
        <p>The <strong>first Drakan encounter</strong> is movement and reaction practice, not a DPS test. Begin with Protect from Melee. His blood marks collect on the side he will swipe; early sparkles show the opposite safe tiles. Move only as his red glow/sound cue commits the lunge, leave a tile behind you, and attack after a successful dodge. Later fights remove the sparkles and add cleaves, waves and blood magic. Quick-escape/resupply if necessary. During the <strong>Blood Hunt</strong>, repair the Sangvesti drawbridge, move between ruins without letting Drakan catch you, fight the feral vyres and Nylocas using the quest's nearby supplies/throwable spines, then escape through the forest and river. Do not substitute a Bowfa grind for learning a telegraph.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Vampyrium supply primer.</strong> The quest's renewable local consumables are for its Vampyrium sections and cannot be banked: <strong>mysterious jerky</strong> is substantial food; <strong>smelly kebabs</strong> are fast food; <strong>foul chunky potions</strong> restore stats/Prayer and add Prayer regeneration; <strong>putrid sticky potions</strong> restore run like stamina; <strong>rank frothy potions</strong> are super-combat boosts; <strong>rancid slimy potions</strong> heal like brews with a small stat drain; and a <strong>jar of congealed blood</strong> fully restores HP and Prayer. Check supply crates/tables at each checkpoint. You do not need to bankroll endless outside brews for these fights.</div>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-flail" number="7" title="Make the deterministic Hallowed flail during Hallowed Preparations">
        <p>At Efaritay's palace, finish the short preparation tasks, then <strong>free seven inventory spaces</strong>. Take the workbench tools, blisterwood logs and blessed silver sickle from the room's crates, and the diamond plus enchant-diamond tablet from its chests. Use the diamond and tablet on the sickle, the logs on the sickle, then use the enchanted blisterwood sickle at the anvil to upgrade your Blisterwood flail into the <strong>Hallowed flail</strong>. Make the required five blisterwood stakes from the supplied logs for the following story beat. This is a <strong>quest-supplied, guaranteed weapon upgrade</strong>, not a vampyre unique hunt.</p>
        <p>The Hallowed flail is <strong>one-handed</strong>, so use the dragon defender with it. Keep Fire Cape, Barrows gloves, Piety and your best sensible melee/defensive armour around that weapon for Drakan. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Hallowed_flail" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Weapon and creation details</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-theatre-wyrd" number="8" title="Finish the Theatre return and Wyrd before the final siege">
        <p>After the palace defence begins, the story returns to Gielinor for <strong>Another Night at the Theatre</strong>. You already learned Entry Mode in 3.4. Bank/regear at Burgh de Rott or Ver Sinhaza: bring ordinary melee, the deterministic crossbow, a Magic attack, food and restores. In the quest's Nylocas waves, match <strong>white/melee, green/ranged, blue/magic</strong> and prioritise dangerous blue targets. Range the <strong>Maiden of Sugadinti</strong> from the south; kill her healing Nylocas at the HP breaks and step off blood pools. The <strong>Nylocas Vasilias</strong> changes colour and attack style: switch protection first, then answer with the matching damage style. These are quest encounters, not a raid-unique check. <strong>Unlike the Vampyrium instances, deaths in this Theatre segment are normal gravestone deaths with possible reclaim fees</strong>; bank a medallion or other return transport and retrieve promptly.</p>
        <p>Next, bank at Burgh de Rott and enter the ruined building north-east of town for <strong>Wyrd</strong>. In melee, Protect from Melee reduces his pushing hits. His repeated cycle has two melee hits, a screech, two hits, another screech and a side-dependent double slam; <strong>turn the overhead off for a screech</strong> and move opposite the arm/side signalled for the slams. At lower HP a bloody screech fills the arena with pools: run out through the opening, keep prayer off until the blast clears, and accept a little pool damage rather than standing in the burst. Ranging from afar avoids his specials but takes unblocked Magic hits; it is an option, not a required weapon swap. Wyrd death returns you outside the lab with items intact, near the Burgh bank. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Blood_Moon_Rises" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Theatre and Wyrd mechanics</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-siege" number="9" title="Hold Drakan's Siege and complete the later story encounter">
        <p>Back at Efaritay's palace, take the <strong>silvthrill ballista and javelins</strong> dropped on the bridge and shoot incoming blood portals. This is a participation/defence sequence, not a normal damage race; keep shooting until the defence advances. Inside, help the aranei recover from falling rubble and respond to cracks in the windows/pillars to keep the hideout standing. Refill from the local supply table before <strong>Drakan's next combat round</strong>. Use the Hallowed flail, Protect from Melee and Piety, and react to the expanded spear/AoE patterns instead of forcing extra hits. Efaritay helps with healing, but you still need to dodge. After the siege, the story returns to Darkmeyer for another assisted Drakan encounter; keep room to step back, dodge the three-swipe sequences and the follow-up orb, and refill before the true final battle. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Blood_Moon_Rises" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Siege and later encounter</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Final mandatory boss · Lowerniel Drakan</div><h2>Read first. Attack second.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i36-drakan" number="10" title="Defeat final Drakan and complete The Blood Moon Rises">
        <p>Follow Efaritay through the graveyard portal back to Vampyrium. At the supply chest by the rooftop door, use the <strong>Hallowed flail + dragon defender, Fire Cape, Barrows gloves, best reasonable melee armour, Protect from Melee and Piety</strong>. Bring a <strong>jar of congealed blood</strong> (one per inventory) as a true emergency full HP/Prayer restore. Fill the rest with local rancid slimy healing, several foul chunky Prayer/stat restores and rank frothy combat boosts; jerky/kebabs are useful simpler food. Putrid sticky stamina is for travel, not this stationary final fight. Refill at the chest between attempts. No Slayer helmet, whip, Bowfa, blowpipe or raid weapon is assumed.</p>
        <p><strong>Phase 1 — swipe and lunge recognition:</strong> watch the side that absorbs his blood marks and move to the opposite safe side when his red cue commits. His spear combos grow from side swipes into slam and front/back or semicircle cleaves; keep a few free tiles behind you and reposition around a corner if a wall removes your dodge. Protect from Melee reduces chip damage, not every special. A successful dodge opens a punish hit—do not greed an attack before the read.</p>
        <p><strong>Phase 2 — blood waves and Magic:</strong> when he disappears and the roof floods, face the incoming walls and <strong>run straight through each wave toward it</strong>; diagonal or spam-clicked pathing often fails. After the final wave, Drakan reappears and fires a cluster of red blood projectiles: activate <strong>Protect from Magic before impact</strong>, then return to Melee protection for his approach/combo. Later single red Magic projectiles need the same brief switch. Do the dodge, take the available punish window, then reset your positioning.</p>
        <p><strong>Phase 3 — pools, lightning and lunges:</strong> avoid blood pools and the lightning's dark floor shadows, both of which can disable your overhead. When Drakan appears to line up the spear lunge, move a few tiles <strong>perpendicular/out of its footprint</strong>, not across the length of his attack. After the lunge sequence, block the returning red projectile cluster with Protect from Magic and resume Melee protection for the combo. The signals speed up across phases. Use one heal or potion between reads, save the jar for a real emergency, and accept a learning attempt rather than chasing a rare DPS upgrade. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Blood_Moon_Rises" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Full current Drakan fight reference</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Retry costs:</strong> in the Vampyrium quest instances, a normal account/standard Ironman who dies keeps their items, respawns near a checkpoint or supply area and pays no ordinary death fee; the final fight returns you to its door with HP/Prayer restored and its supply chest available, but restarts at phase 1. Teleporting away requires returning through the Icyene Graveyard portal. <strong>Hardcore Ironmen still lose status on death.</strong> This does not override the Theatre segment's ordinary gravestone rules above. Learn the missed mechanic, refill, and retry.</p>
        <p>On completion, record <strong>4 Quest Points, Vampyrium access, the Hallowed flail and Sunspear, Maggot King access, new Vampyrium skilling/Slayer options and the restored Burgh de Rott pub</strong>. The repeatable Maggot King and its uniques are <em>not</em> part of graduation. The reward <strong>tome of experience has six uses of 30,000 XP</strong> on an eligible skill <em>over level 70</em>; it can select the same skill repeatedly and be reclaimed from Efaritay at Castle Drakan if saved. All Quest Cape entry gates are already behind you, so <strong>do not spend or count this tome in prerequisite arithmetic</strong>. Choose its allocation for whatever post-guide direction you actually enjoy.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">The final journal check</div><h2>Let the live game, not a static list, decide whether the cape is ready.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i36-journal" number="11" title="Confirm every currently released quest is green">
        <p>Sort/filter the quest journal and confirm <strong>every currently released quest is green</strong>. The route's September 2026 coverage includes <strong>The Ides of Milk, The Red Reef, The Blood Moon Rises, Fallen From Grace, A Ruff Situation and Crab Quest</strong>, alongside the older quest cleanup and Grandmasters in 3.5. Learning the Ropes was Tutorial Island. Do not add announced but unreleased quests. If a quest released after publication, finish it before buying or wearing the cape; follow its actual new requirements rather than inventing a Chapter 3.7. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Quests/List" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current quest list</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-cape" number="12" title="Buy the Quest point cape and hood — graduate">
        <p>With the journal all green, take <strong>99,000 coins</strong> to the <strong>Wise Old Man in Draynor Village</strong> and purchase the <strong>Quest point cape and hood</strong>. A new released quest will suspend the ability to wear/use the cape until completed. This purchase, together with the Fire Cape already earned in 3.3, ends the Intermediate guide's mandatory linear route. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Quest_point_cape" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cape ownership and purchase</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">Intermediate Guide Complete · choose your own direction</div>
        <h3>Quest Cape and Fire Cape earned. The route is yours now.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Guaranteed capes and combat:</strong> current Quest point cape and hood, Fire Cape/Jad, Barrows gloves, Piety, dragon defender and the deterministic Hallowed flail.</li>
          <li><strong>Guaranteed world and travel:</strong> Prifddinas, Vampyrium, fairy rings, Kingdom access, Drakan's medallion, Royal seed pod, Ring of shadows, the useful house/lectern/tablet network, and Ancient, Lunar and Arceuus spellbook infrastructure.</li>
          <li><strong>Guaranteed quest experience:</strong> While Guthix Sleeps, Monkey Madness II, Theatre Entry, Dragon Slayer II, Desert Treasure II and The Blood Moon Rises, with the full currently released quest journal green.</li>
          <li><strong>Not guaranteed or required:</strong> Bowfa/full crystal, Ava's assembler, Slayer helmet, whip, trident, zenytes, blowpipe, raid uniques, ornate/max POH, diary cape or a high Combat Achievement tier.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section><div class="section-label">Where do I go now? · optional, unranked</div><h2>Pick a path because it sounds fun.</h2>
        <p>These are directions, not another mandatory chapter or a ranked shopping list. <strong>Gauntlet/crystal</strong> can be a resumable Bowfa project if you enjoy it. <strong>Slayer</strong> can build toward black mask/helmet, whip, zenytes and higher levels. <strong>Vorkath</strong> can supply the optional head for Ava's assembler; <strong>Zulrah</strong> offers a separate scales/blowpipe/unique hunt. <strong>Raids</strong> can begin with low-invocation Tombs of Amascut, already unlocked by Beneath Cursed Sands. <strong>Vampyrium</strong> offers bloodwood, skilling, Slayer and Maggot King. Or build <strong>account infrastructure</strong> through POH conveniences, diaries, Combat Achievements and teleports, or just pursue relaxed skills, clues and a collection log. None of these paths supplies a missing graduation checkbox.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
    <aside class="sidebar right-rail"><ProgressTracker storageKey="rsag-intermediate-3-6" title="3.6 progress" /></aside>
    <IntermediatePager previousHref={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-5/`} previousLabel="← 3.5" />
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
